<BaseLayout title="About | Aging at Home Lab" description="About Aging at Home Lab and our practical, trust-first approach to aging-in-place guidance.">
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>We make aging-in-place decisions clearer, calmer, and more practical.</h1>
    <p>Aging at Home Lab is a practical publishing project for families helping older adults stay safer and more supported at home.</p>
    <p>Our focus is not generic inspiration. We build checklists, templates, decision guides, and plain-English explainers for the moments when families need to make real choices about home safety, care organization, emergency readiness, and aging-in-place support.</p>

    <h2>What we cover</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Room-by-room home safety checklists</li>
      <li>Caregiver binders and organization tools</li>
      <li>Medication and appointment tracking templates</li>
      <li>Medical alert and senior-tech decision guides</li>
      <li>Home modification questions to ask professionals</li>
      <li>Family communication and care coordination tools</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Our trust stance</h2>
    <p>This site provides general education and organization tools. It does not provide personalized medical, legal, financial, construction, or safety advice.</p>
    <p>When a topic affects health, medications, legal authority, home modifications, or personal safety, we aim to clearly explain when readers should involve qualified professionals.</p>

    <h2>Our north star</h2>
    <p>If an overwhelmed family member lands on one of our pages after something scary happened, the page should help them breathe, understand what matters, and take the next sane step.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
